  "id": "Compound::DB01159 - Gene::2562",
  "verbalization": "Halothane appears to interact with Gabrb3 through a shared pathway involving Gaba receptor activity. The evidence suggests that Halothane binds to Gabra6 or Gabra4, which then participates in Gaba receptor activity, ultimately leading to the participation of Gabrb3. This indicates a potential mechanism where Halothane may influence Gabrb3 through a common intermediary in the GABA signaling pathway. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with the highest score supporting the interaction through Gabra6. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Halothane in modulating GABA receptor function, potentially through the activation of Gabrb3. The observed overlap in the involvement of Gabra subunits in GABA receptor activity supports a mechanism where Halothane may exert its effects on Gabrb3 via a shared regulatory pathway.",
